[h1]R.A.T.S. Flotilla[/h1]
[i]R.A.T.S. – Reconnaissance, Acoustics, Terrain & Signals[/i]
[b]Bugs, ideas, questions:[/b] [url=https://hub.sewerlabs.dev/s/flotilla]R.A.T.S. feedback board[/url]

[b]A test bench for Sea Power: several installs side by side, each with its own mods, settings and saves.[/b]
Is that bug the game or a mod? Check it on a bone-clean install. Does this giant mod list even start? Find out without touching your Steam install. Did the update break something? Keep the older version next to the new one and compare.

[list]
[*][b]Bug reports[/b]: reproduce it on a clean install with no mods and no loader, so the developers get a report they can use
[*][b]Testing mod sets[/b]: load one copy to the gills while your everyday game stays as it is
[*][b]Modders[/b]: try a build on its own copy, against the game version you pick
[/list]

[b]This is a small Windows app, not a game mod.[/b] Subscribing brings it to your PC; switching it on in the game's Mods menu does nothing, so leave it off.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]New copy[/b]: Clean (only the game's own files, no mod loader, no mods, fresh settings) or a copy of your whole setup. About 19 GB each
[*][b]Play[/b]: starts the copy you pick, with its own settings, load order and saves
[*][b]Mods[/b]: for one copy, switch mods on or off, set their order, or add a mod from a folder or .zip to that copy alone. Shows which game version each mod was made for
[*][b]Keep in this copy[/b]: freeze a Workshop mod in one copy. Steam updates no longer change it there, the other copies still update. [b]Use Workshop again[/b] goes back
[*][b]Rename[/b]: call a copy what it is for
[*][b]Update[/b]: after a game update, refresh a copy's game files and keep its mods and saves. Or don't, and keep the older version around
[*][b]Desktop shortcut[/b] for any copy, and [b]Delete[/b] when you are done with it
[/list]

[h2]Start it[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe and let Steam download it
[*]Open [i]steamapps\workshop\content\1286220[/i] in the Steam library that holds Sea Power, then the folder named after the number at the end of this page's address
[*]Start [b]SeaPowerFlotilla.exe[/b] once. It moves to a safe place on your PC and offers a desktop shortcut; from then on start it from there. New versions from the Workshop are picked up by themselves
[/olist]
Windows may say "unknown publisher": More info, then Run anyway. No admin rights needed. Needs .NET Framework 4.8, which every Windows 10 and 11 has. Prefer a plain download? It is also on [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerFlotilla/releases]GitHub[/url].

Step by step: the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3836683383]Flotilla guide[/url].

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*]Workshop subscriptions belong to your Steam account, so every copy sees them. Which ones are switched on, and in what order, is kept per copy. For a copy with its own version of a mod, use Keep in this copy
[*]Mods with scripts need a mod loader in that copy: Keel or Anchor Chain, either one. A Clean copy has none, on purpose
[*]One Sea Power at a time. While a copy runs, don't start the game from your Steam library
[*]Your Steam install is never changed. While a copy runs, the game's data folder is switched to the copy's and put back when the game closes
[*]Steam updates only its own install, and copies are not synced to Steam Cloud
[/list]

Source and details: [url=https://github.com/struckl/SeaPowerFlotilla]GitHub[/url]. MIT License. Not affiliated with Triassic Games or MicroProse.

[i]R.A.T.S. – Ratte's Assorted Tactical Systems[/i]
